---

4. Development Process

Step 1: Frontend Development

The user interface is developed first. It contains:

Login/Register page

Home/Dashboard

AI Chat interface

Study material section

Summary generator

Quiz section

Profile section


The interface is designed to be simple so that students can easily access different learning features.


---

Step 2: Backend Development

The backend handles the main application logic.

It is responsible for:

Processing user requests

Connecting the frontend with the Gemini API

Managing user information

Processing learning content

Sending AI-generated responses to the user

Handling errors and authentication


Python can be used to create the backend because it provides simple integration with AI services.


---

Step 3: Gemini AI Integration

The Google Gemini API is integrated into EduGenie to provide AI-powered learning assistance.

Basic workflow:

Student enters question
        ↓
EduGenie Frontend
        ↓
Backend
        ↓
Google Gemini API
        ↓
AI processes the question
        ↓
Response returned to Backend
        ↓
Response displayed to Student

For example:

Student:
"What is normalization in DBMS?"

EduGenie:
"Normalization is a database design technique used to organize data and reduce data redundancy."

The system can also provide longer explanations when required.


